References:

     Box, G. E. P. and Cox, D. R. (1964) An analysis of
     transformations. _JRSS B_ *26* 211-246.

     Guerrero, V.M. (1993) Time-series analysis supported by power
     transformations. _Journal of Forecasting_, *12*, 37-48.

See Also:

     'BoxCox()'

Examples:

     lambda <- BoxCox.lambda(AirPassengers, lower = 0) 
     adf.test(x, alternative = c("stationary", "explosive"),
alternative: indicates the alternative hypothesis and must be one of
          '"stationary"' (default) or '"explosive"'. You can specify
     computed. The p-values are interpolated from Table 4.2, p. 103 of
alternative: a character string describing the alternative hypothesis.
== M8 apoyo: forecast::BoxCox admite negativos con lambda > 0 ==
{
    if (lambda == "auto") {
        lambda <- BoxCox.lambda(x, lower = -0.9)
    }
    if (lambda < 0) {
        x[x < 0] <- NA
    }
    if (lambda == 0) {
        out <- log(x)
    }
    else {
        out <- (sign(x) * abs(x)^lambda - 1)/lambda
    }
    if (!is.null(colnames(x))) {
        colnames(out) <- colnames(x)
    }
    attr(out, "lambda") <- lambda
    out
}
